I stopped wishing for artifacts at some point.  They are too
easy to get without wishing with two each lawfull and chaotic
easily generated without wishing plus altar dancing for the
co-aligned and un-aligned ones.  Having a couple of neutral
artifacts easily generated in the game might be nice as well -
In the midgame as the chaotic ones are easy in the early
game and the lawfull ones easy in the late game currently.

> Does NetHack have a limit on artifact *generation*? I thought this
> limit only applied to artifact *wishing*.

Getting artifacts as gifts has an exponential roll off so yes
there is a limit.  Long before you have them all it starts to
take thousands of sacrifices to get the next one.  Getting
artifacts in bones files has its own way of ending up self
limited.

As to being generated on the floor, that's rare enough the
limits exist because of the limited size and number of
levels.   Hmmm, I've never seen an artifact generated as
a death drop but the longest I've ever pudding danced was
until I got all of the intrinsics from eating them.  Do death
drops ever get converted to artifacts?  I have the sources
downloaded lately so I could check the source.

> Wouldn't a stricter restriction of artifact wishing or a prohibition
> of wishing for quest artifacts of other classes be something that
> would fit SporkHacks design concept?

There's been plenty of discussion about banning wishing
for Quest artifacts.  Having such a wish get an extra 4-in-5
failure rate independent of the existance of other artifacts
might work, but plenty of players simply don't wish for Quest
artifacts.


